<Defs>

  <!--
    Deeds: what colonists do that the others talk about (ColonyCouncil.DeedDef, Source/ColonyCouncil/Social/Gossip/).
    facets: how it reflects on the doer, per side of a name, for a deed of size 1 (courage, kindness, diligence, skill,
    discretion, temper; temper up is a hothead). text: what they did, without the doer ({SUBJECT_...} is the doer,
    {VICTIM} the other person in it by name, {DETAIL} a detail from the hook); textAlone without anyone else in it.
    Speech lines put the text after the doer's name (and a boast after "I"), so keep it short (under 45 letters or
    so) and don't refer back to the doer in it.
    Triggers: memories (the game gives the one it was done to a memory about the doer), historyEvents (the game names
    the doer), mentalStates (the doer starts one), encounters (Rimfolk's moments with strangers). Deeds without
    triggers are recorded by hooks in the code (fights won, contests, secrets, elections, fine work, ambitions, the
    council meeting, idling, tending, gossiping). Names that aren't in this game (a DLC not loaded) are never met.
  -->

  <!-- ===================== Fights ===================== -->

